Weather CLI

A simple Node.js command-line tool to fetch current weather information for any city using the [OpenWeatherMap API](https://openweathermap.org/).


Features:

- Get real-time weather data by city name
- Shows:
  - Temperature (°C)
  - Feels like temperature
  - Weather conditions
  - Humidity
  - Wind speed
- Handles invalid city names with friendly error messages


Requirements:
  -[Node.js] on terminal  

Installation :

Clone the repository:

```bash

git clone https://github.com/srikesav09/weather-cli.git
cd weather-cli 
```
    To access the git repo using the command prompt.
```bash
npm install
```
    Install npm to execute the Weather-cli in the command prompt.

```bash
    chmod +x index.js
```
    For Linux or Macos , use this command to execute the file.

Note:
    If executing using npm then use 
```bash 
npm start -- <city_name>
```
    city_name - The name of the city you want the weather reort on.

